2026-09-23 — K01 phase-bounded static-key diagnostic. K01 remains OPEN.

The four-reader signed module adds publication-phase observations to the
earlier static-key/RCU reduction. It never frees or dereferences the object.
The writer publishes, enables, disables, waits for synchronize_rcu, then clears
the pointer, in 256 rounds. Reader phase observations use READ_ONCE, not a new
barrier. reader_preempt=1 additionally forbids preemption across the read-side
critical section; memory_gate=1 uses an acquire/release Boolean instead of
instruction patching. The same module and payload are used in all six boots.

Actual missing-pointer counts (static / memory / preemption-disabled):
                        GCC reference            EvoCC subject
TCG Cortex-A72, MT       753386 / 0 / 1188348       549995 / 0 / 485852
HVF host                     0 / 0 / 0                 0 / 0 / 0
TCG Cortex-A72, single        0 / 0 / 0                 0 / 0 / 0
Every mode completes 256 rounds with four readers and millions of actual
reads. Both kernels boot and shut down in all three lanes. The TCG MT static
and preemption-disabled program verdicts are FAIL; the other 14 are PASS.

All but two stable MT reference observations, and all stable MT subject
observations, occur in phase 7: disable completed, grace period returned and
pointer cleared. There are also 1 reference / 7 subject changing-phase
observations across the two failing modes. Initial bad-event snapshots show
the branch instruction as NOP (d503201f), enabled count zero, RCU nesting one.
The observations narrow the discrepancy to concurrent branch publication in
this MT-TCG environment. They do not yet prove a specific emulator defect or
that it is the cause of the original sched_ext NULL dereference. No production
kernel code, acceptance contract, watchdog or full-run verdict was changed.
The earlier single-thread original sched_ext run timed out; these small-case
passes do not supersede it or close K01.

Build reuses sched-static-key-lifetime-load.c, the matching reference kernel
headers/signing certificate and the existing initramfs init. The module object
name stays sched-static-key-lifetime.ko so the same loader is used. Three static
GCC loaders differ only by MODULE_PARAMETERS: empty, memory_gate=1,
reader_preempt=1. Each test has 90 seconds, outer boot bound 330 seconds.
GCC 14.2.0-19 builds this diagnostic infrastructure on both kernel subjects;
none of this adds EvoCC target-C compilation credit. Commands/environment are
the same external-module/sign-file/gen_init_cpio path recorded in
sched-static-key-lifetime.out. Source/kernel mounts are read-only, network off.

Flights use tools/k1/selftest.py flight -> tools/k1/boot.sh, four CPUs, 2048 MiB,
K1_ALLOW_QEMU_DRIFT=1 and K1_KUNIT_AUTORUN=0. tcg-cortex-a72 and hvf-host are
existing lanes; the single-thread diagnostic copies the contract under .build
and changes only acceleration to tcg,thread=single, keeping cortex-a72. It is
marked diagnostic-only, never the locked acceptance contract. All use the
existing 64 MiB snapshot scratch disk, not a copied full runtime disk.

