2026-09-26 — Direct-block-chaining negative control (diagnostic only).
The same source/module/payload/Images were replayed with MT TCG Cortex-A72
and only QEMU's `-d nochain` added in a separate diagnostic contract. Local
QEMU help identifies this option as disabling direct block chaining. CPU/RAM,
program bounds and the original locked acceptance contracts are unchanged.

Missing pointers (static / memory / preemption-disabled):
GCC reference       273139 / 0 / 335854
EvoCC subject       105318 / 0 / 148643
Both boot/shutdown verdicts are PASS; each has two program FAILs and one PASS.
All programs finish the original 256 rounds. Disabling direct block chaining
does not remove the discrepancy; it is neither a remedy nor evidence that
chaining is its necessary cause. The emulator attribution and causal link to
the original sched_ext fault remain unproved. K01 stays OPEN.

Added command: -accel tcg,thread=multi -cpu cortex-a72 -d nochain
nochain.py reuses the same 64 MiB snapshot scratch disk; no runtime disk copy.
